From: zibao <zibao@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: sunxi: stop the counter across system sleep

The sunxi watchdog counter is clocked from the always-on domain: it keeps
counting while the system is in s2idle, while the only task pinging it is
userspace, which is frozen for the whole sleep.  The board is therefore
reset in the middle of the sleep instead of resuming it.

watchdog_dev_suspend(), the core PM notifier, is not enough on its own: it
pings once on PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE and cancels the ping worker, but it never
stops the hardware.  The driver has to stop the counter, and restart it on
resume.

Set WDOG_NO_PING_ON_SUSPEND so the core coordinates the sleep, store the
driver data (probe never called platform_set_drvdata()), and add PM ops
that call sunxi_wdt_stop()/sunxi_wdt_start() around the sleep.  The ops
only act when the watchdog is active, i.e. opened by userspace.

Measured on a H96 Max H618 (H618, 16 s timeout, s2idle) on 2026-11-26:
a 90 s sleep reset the board after 16 s, while an 8 s sleep resumed
cleanly.  With this change the counter is disabled for the whole sleep
and reprogrammed with the same timeout on resume.

Signed-off-by: zibao <zibao@proton.me>

--- a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
@@ -192,6 +192,28 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int __maybe_unused sunxi_wdt_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct sunxi_wdt_dev *sunxi_wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (watchdog_active(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev))
+		sunxi_wdt_stop(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused sunxi_wdt_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct sunxi_wdt_dev *sunxi_wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (watchdog_active(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev))
+		sunxi_wdt_start(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(sunxi_wdt_pm_ops, sunxi_wdt_suspend, sunxi_wdt_resume);
+
 static const struct watchdog_info sunxi_wdt_info = {
 	.identity	= DRV_NAME,
 	.options	= WDIOF_SETTIMEOUT |
@@ -286,6 +308,14 @@
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, sunxi_wdt);
 
+	/*
+	 * The counter is clocked from the always-on domain and cannot be
+	 * serviced while the system is suspended.  Let the core stop its ping
+	 * worker before the sleep, and stop the counter itself in ->suspend().
+	 */
+	set_bit(WDOG_NO_PING_ON_SUSPEND, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.status);
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, sunxi_wdt);
+
 	sunxi_wdt_stop(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
 
 	watchdog_stop_on_reboot(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
@@ -304,6 +334,7 @@
 	.driver		= {
 		.name		= DRV_NAME,
 		.of_match_table	= sunxi_wdt_dt_ids,
+		.pm		= &sunxi_wdt_pm_ops,
 	},
 };
 
